# Sort keys: transform + comparator implementation in the module 39 zero cave.
name: sortkeys-cave
kind: module
module: 39
region: code
address: 0x0309f000
gate: build refuses unless the stock bytes at the target equal `expect`;
  the finished image must also pass firmware_patch.validate()
rationale: Installs the sort-key implementation (cave_cmp, cave_pfx,
  sk_str_addr, sk_tcmp, sk_pfx4, gen_init, gen_next, sk_fold
  and the 128-byte Latin-1 fold table) into the zero region
  at the tail of module 39's code span (real code ends at
  0x0307e1ec; span ends 0x0309f4ac; an overlap scan over all
  82 modules' code/data/bss spans showed only module 39's own
  code covers 0x0309f000..0x0309f41c, and the stock bytes
  there are all zero, which is what `expect` pins). Blob is
  1052 of the 1196 available bytes. Verified offline: host
  reference suite (vectors + 4000-pair ordering fuzz) and a
  Unicorn differential test of sk_tcmp / sk_pfx4 against the
  host model over 349 names, 0 failures; see
  work/patches/sort_keys/sort_keys.md. Source:
  work/patches/sort_keys/sortkey_asm.py (assembled with
  rz-asm; cmp.w is used for every r12 immediate compare
  because rz-asm silently truncates `cmp r12, #imm` to r4).
